<title>USA: USDA extends comment period for cotton rules.</title>
<headline>USDA extends comment period for cotton rules.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department's Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service said Tuesday it would extend the public comment period until April 30 for a rulemaking on cotton imports.</p>
<p>Last December, the agency began a rulemaking for changes to regulations for importing cotton into the United States.</p>
<p>A notice published in the Federal Register on Tuesday said that the National Cotton Council asked the Agriculture Department to extend the comment period beyond the original March 31 deadline.</p>
<p>((-- Washington commodities desk, 202-898-8300))</p>
